    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/gymnogeophagus_meridionalis_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>Almost a dwarf cichlid. Specimens bred in ponds in Germany are 5–7 cm long, fully mature and in colour. Origin: captive-bred.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/gymnogeophagus_meridionalis_en-2/",
      "html": "<p>There is still no agreement among specialized aquarists whether this form represents a population of Gymnogeophagus meridionalis, G. rhabdotus or a still undescribed new species. In the literature this population is also named \"Gymnogeophagus sp. Rosario II\" or \"Gymnogeophagus sp. Arco Iris\".</p><p>Lexicon: Gymnogeophagus: from ancient Greek, means \"naked Geophagus\", referring to the unscaled snout. Geophagus is another genus of cichlid. meridionalis: Latin, means \"southern\". rhabdotus: from ancient Greek, means \"striped\".</p><p>Suggestion of a common name: Small rainbow eartheater.</p>"
    }
  ],
